{ Let's start !! Play e4.. }
1. e4 c6 { Do you remember what to play ? } 2. d4 d5 { Now ? } 3. Nd2 { [%cal Gd2e4,Ge4g5,Gg5f7] } 3... dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nf6 { Is the sacrifice coming closer ? What will you play? } 5. Ng5 h6 { Sacrifice thaaa Knight!! } 6. Nxf7!! Kxf7 { Now we are going to make some developing moves.. Play Nf3. } 7. Nf3 Nbd7 { Nd7 is controlling e5 so we cannot give a check. Still we can give a check, can you find it? } { [%csl Ge5][%cal Gd7e5,Gf3e5] } 8. Bc4+ Ke8 { Black has four options to play e6, ke8 , Nd5 or kg6. Let's say the opponent played ke8. We can castle to make our king safe. } 9. O-O Nb6 { We will play Bd3 to control the empty diagonal and make our bishop safe. } 10. Bd3 { [%csl Gd3][%cal Gd3h7] } 10... Bg4?? { Black pinned our knight, so what we can still move it. Ne5! (TOP ENGINE MOVE)Sacrificing thaaa Queeeen! Do you know why? The stockfish gives white an advantage of +4.0. } { [%csl Gf3,Ge5,Gd1,Gg6][%cal Gf3e5,Gg4d1,Gd3g6] } 11. Ne5!! Bxd1?? { Bxd1 is a BLUNDER can you find why? } 12. Bg6#! *


