{ Initiate the Alien Gambit!!😤😤 }
1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nf6 5. Ng5 h6 { Now I think you are familiar with this opening? 🤔🧐 } 6. Nxf7!! Kxf7 { Remember what developing move we played in the previous chapter ?🤔 } 7. Nf3 Bf5 { The opponent played Bf5.. We are going to give a check with the Knight.. (Ne5+ is common move played in most of the traps)👍💪 } 8. Ne5+ { [%cal Gf7e8,Gf7g8,Gf7e6] } 8... Kg8 { We saw in the earlier trap that King went to e8 now it is going to g8..(Kg8 has been played in 9,500+ games). Let's see the trap further. Give him a check..✅👍 } 9. Bc4+ e6? { Here to defend the check the top engine move is Nd5 but lets say the opponent does not finds it and plays e6( e6 played in 4,500+ games). Winrate of 63% for white.🙂👍
There is a 20% chance that black plays Nd5(TOP ENGINE MOVE) Can you find a way to win the pawn? } (9... Kh7 10. g4 Be4 11. g5 hxg5 12. Nf7! { [%cal Gf7g5,Gf7h8,Gf7d8] } 12... Qd7 13. Nxg5+ Kg6 14. Bf7+ Kh6 15. Nxe4+ Kh7 16. Nxf6+ gxf6 (16... exf6 17. Qh5#) 17. Qh5+ Bh6 18. Qxh6#) 10. g4! { Moves the Bishop away from the defense of the pawn.( g4 has been played in7,500+ games). Winrate of 75% for white.💪✅👍 } 10... Be4 { Capture the free pawn (Bxe6+).. } { [%cal Ge4h1] } 11. Bxe6+ Kh7 { Here we will play g5 ( Played in 450+ games and giving a winrate of 78% for white).Can you guess why? Giving the rook for free.. } 12. g5! { Black can either play Qe7, hxg5, Bxh1?? or Bb4+(TOP ENGINE MOVE).
*If Bb4+ then we reply with c3.
*If Qe7 , Bb3 , hxg5, Bxh1 ,Qd3+ ,Be4 , Qh3+ ,Nh5 , Qxh5#.
*These moves are played very rarely. Qe7 has 7% chances and Bb4+ 2% chances to be played. } 12... Bxh1?? { Bxh1 is BLUNDER , Can you tell why? } (12... Qe7 13. Bb3 hxg5 14. Bxg5 Bxh1?? { [%cal Gd1d3,Gh1e4,Gd3h3,Gf6h5,Gh3h5] } 15. Qd3+ Be4 16. Qh3+ Nh5 17. Qxh5#) (12... hxg5 13. Nf7! { [%cal Gf7d8,Gf7h8,Gf7g5] } 13... Qa5+ 14. Bd2) (12... Bb4+ 13. c3 Re8 14. Bb3 Rxe5 (14... Bxh1 15. g6+ Kh8)) 13. g6#! { A pawn checkmate isn't amazing!! } *


