[UTCTime "05:47:15"]
[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

{ Let's start .. This trap was played between Witty Alien, and a GM and Witty Alien won the game, in the following manner. Start by playing e4. }
1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nf6 5. Ng5 h6 6. Nxf7!! Kxf7 7. Nf3 Nbd7 { Nd7 is controlling d6 so we can't give a check with the Knight. We will develop the bishop by playing Bd3. } { [%csl Ge5][%cal Gd7e5,Gf3e5] } 8. Bd3 { [%csl Gg6][%cal Gd3g6] } 8... e6 { Now we will Castle.Making the king safe. } 9. O-O Bd6 { Bring the rook to the open file. } 10. Re1 Re8? { Play Ne5+ to make the Queen' s diagnol empty. } 11. Ne5+! Bxe5?? { This is a BLUNDER, as now we retake with the pawn and black's knight is under attack. After the knight moves the h5 square is undefended so we play Qh5+!. Bxe5?? gives white an advantage of +1.8 by the stockfish. } 12. dxe5 { Here the TOP ENGINE MOVE for black is Kg8 sacrificing the knight. But Kg8 is not possible for a human to find it until and unless the player is cheating. } { [%csl Gh5][%cal Gd1h5] } 12... Nd5?! { Play Qh5+ giving a check to black. } 13. Qh5+! Kg8 { Here comes the BRILLIANT BISHOP SACRIFICE, can you find it is a little difficult. } 14. Bxh6!! { This move has been played in over 900+ games. } 14... gxh6?? { If the pawn take we have a MATE IN 6.. Play Qg6+. } (14... Nf8 15. Bxg7!! Kxg7 16. Re4 Ng6 17. Rg4 Nf4 18. Rxg6+!! Nxg6 19. Qxg6+ Kh8 (19... Kf8 20. Qh6+ { [%cal Gf8f7,Gf8g8,Gf8e7] } 20... Ke7 (20... Kg8 21. Qh7+ Kf8 22. Bg6 { [%cal Ge8e7,Gd8d7] } 22... Re7 (22... Qd7 23. Qh8+ Ke7 24. Qf6#) 23. Qh8#) (20... Kf7 21. Bg6+ { [%cal Gf7e7,Gf7g8] } 21... Kg8 (21... Ke7 22. Qg7#) 22. Qh7+ Kf8 23. Qf7#) 21. Qg7#) 20. Qh7#) 15. Qg6+ { If black plays Kh8 we have Qh7#. } { [%cal Gg8h8] } 15... Kf8 { Capture the pawn. } (15... Kh8 16. Qh7#) 16. Qxh6+ { If Ke7 we will play Qh7#. } 16... Kg8 { Can you find the MATING SEQUENCE? } (16... Ke7 17. Qg7#) (16... Kf7 17. Bg6+ Kg8 (17... Ke7 18. Qg7#) 18. Qh7+ Kf8 19. Qf7#) 17. Bh7+ Kh8 18. Bg6+ Kg8 19. Qh7+ Kf8 { Find the MATE. } 20. Qf7# { All the mating variations are explained in my blog on Alien Gambit. Check it out
( lichess.org/@/ishaan_biswas/blog/crush-the-caro-kann-defense-with-the-alian-gambit/4yIWRNkj ) } *


