{ Start the Gambit!! }
1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nf6 5. Ng5 h6 6. Nxf7!! Kxf7 7. Nf3 e6 { Give a check. } 8. Ne5+ Kg8 { The black king went in the corner to be safe now we are going to play Bd3 controlling the diagnol. } 9. Bd3 { [%cal Gd3h7] } 9... Bd6 { We are now going to play f4 to anchor the knight on e5, even if the opponent takes the knight we will have a good pawn structure. } 10. f4 Bxe5?? { Capture with the f pawn.. } 11. fxe5 { If black takes the free pawn of d4 with the queen we have Bh7+!!.Winning the queen. } 11... Nd5 { Castling making our king safe and bringing the rook to an open file. } (11... Qxd4?? 12. Bh7+!! Nxh7 13. Qxd4) 12. O-O { [%cal Gf1f8] } 12... Nd7 { Now we are going to play Bg6 to make some mating possibilities. } 13. Bg6 Nf8 { After Nf8, we will play Bf7+ threating MATE.. } 14. Bf7+ Kh7 { Can you find the winning move ? } 15. Qd3+ g6 { Can you find the BRILLIANT MOVE ? } 16. Bxg6+!! Nxg6?? { Can you find why Nxg6 is BLUNDER ? } 17. Rf7+ Kg8 { Find MATE IN 1. } 18. Qxg6# *


