1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nf6 5. Ng5 h6 6. Nxf7!! Kxf7 7. Nf3 Bg4?? { Bg4 looks like a natural move but it is a BLUNDER.. Can you find the winning move ? } 8. Ne5+! { [%cal Ge5g4,Ge5f7,Gf7g8] } 8... Ke8 (8... Kg8 9. Bc4+ Kh7?? 10. Qd3+! Bf5 11. Qxf5+ g6 12. Qxg6#) 9. Nxg4 { Here you might question that Bc4 is threatening mate so why cannot play it? It is because black has Qa5+ making an escape square on d8 and after we play Bd2 black can sacrifice thaa Queen , Qxe5+ , dxe5 then Black takes our queen Bxd1 and we are completely lost. } (9. Bc4?? { Black has Qa5+ making an escape square on d8. } 9... Bxd1?? (9... Qa5+! 10. Bd2 (10. Qd2 Qxd2+ 11. Kxd2) 10... Qxe5+!! 11. dxe5 Bxd1 12. Rxd1) 10. Bf7#!) *


