{ This position is when you accept the Alian Gambit, as black. }
1. Nf3 { We know that c5 is the TOP ENGINE MOVE as if white takes the pawn we take trade Queens and now there is a less chance of getting mated. } 1... c5! 2. Bc4+ { Block the check by playing e6. } 2... e6 3. Ne5+ { Play Kg8. } 3... Kg8 4. c3 { Develop the knight on c6 attacking the d4 pawn } 4... Nc6 5. Ng6 { Here do not make a mistake by playing Rh7 as the rook is useless in this position and our opponent's Knight is very vulnerable, it would be bad for our opponent if white captures our useless rook. Instead play cxd4. } 5... cxd4 (5... Rh7??) 6. Nxh8? { Take the Knight.. } 6... Kxh8 7. cxd4 { Here do not take the pawn first play Bb4+ and white wouldn't move the king to lose their castling rights, but play Bd2. } 7... Bb4+ 8. Bd2 { Now we can take the free pawn with the queen. } 8... Qxd4 { I hope that you have liked this study. I hope that I have not disappointed you as this is my first study. Please leave a like ❤️ if you like this study and want me to make more studies like this.Do try this Gambit 👽.. } *


